**Summary**

No separate upstream `verified-node-replication` checkout or matching `cyclicbuffer.rs` was found in the available filesystem. The only relevant files are the task input and its generated counterpart: `/workspace/task_env/cyclicbuffer_full.rs` and `/workspace/task_env/cyclicbuffer_full_verified.rs`. The verified counterpart contains partial inductive proof bodies that are useful as templates, but several inductive proofs and helper lemmas remain empty. I could not query internet sources because no internet/GitHub fetch tool is exposed in this environment.

**Available Matching Files**

- `/workspace/task_env/cyclicbuffer_full.rs` — self-contained adaptation of `verified-node-replication/src/spec/cyclicbuffer.rs`; the provenance comment appears at lines 1-4.
- `/workspace/task_env/cyclicbuffer_full_verified.rs` — corresponding proof-annotated adaptation; the same provenance comment appears at lines 1-4.
- `/workspace/task_env/session/session-state/920fb2ba-2670-4d96-8de0-30962227cb1b/rewind-file-snapshots/backups/93f5f4d042706c14fde61d43dcfaf8eaad62b6ced857321827007d517a10e24a` — earlier snapshot of the unproved version, not an independent source.

**Useful Proof Bodies**

`advance_head_finish_inductive` in `/workspace/task_env/cyclicbuffer_full_verified.rs:675-688` establishes the relevant pre-state invariants, extracts the combiner state, proves the replica scan completed, invokes the minimum-map lemma, and establishes the minimum local version bound:

```rust
#[inductive(advance_head_finish)]
fn advance_head_finish_inductive(pre: Self, post: Self, node_id: NodeId) {
    assert(pre.pointer_ordering());
    assert(pre.pointer_differences());
    assert(pre.complete());
    assert(pre.all_combiner_valid());
    assert(pre.combiner.contains_key(node_id));
    assert(pre.combiner[node_id].is_AdvancingHead());
    let idx = pre.combiner[node_id].get_AdvancingHead_idx();
    let min_local_version =
        pre.combiner[node_id].get_AdvancingHead_min_local_version();
    assert(idx == pre.num_replicas);
    map_min_value_smallest(
        pre.local_versions,
        (pre.num_replicas - 1) as nat
    );
    assert(min_local_version <= pre.local_versions[0]);
}
```

`advance_tail_start_inductive` in `/workspace/task_env/cyclicbuffer_full_verified.rs:690-694` uses pointer ordering and combiner validity:

```rust
#[inductive(advance_tail_start)]
fn advance_tail_start_inductive(pre: Self, post: Self, node_id: NodeId) {
    assert(pre.pointer_ordering());
    assert(pre.all_combiner_valid());
}
```

`advance_tail_finish_inductive` in `/workspace/task_env/cyclicbuffer_full_verified.rs:699-711` preserves buffer/content invariants and invokes `map_min_value_smallest`:

```rust
#[inductive(advance_tail_finish)]
fn advance_tail_finish_inductive(
    pre: Self,
    post: Self,
    node_id: NodeId,
    new_tail: nat,
) {
    assert(pre.complete());
    assert(pre.inv_buffer_contents());
    assert(pre.contents_meet_inv());
    assert(pre.all_combiner_valid());
    assert(pre.pointer_ordering());
    assert(pre.pointer_differences());
